        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "96e52e06-381d-3d2d-bbee-33ce13a1ec42",
                "word": "onagre",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5337f4f4-2b45-4cac-8d5e-106ee7ce2854",
                        "entry_id": "96e52e06-381d-3d2d-bbee-33ce13a1ec42",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "onagres"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d211b040-64ed-3237-bf44-d7648c9fd8f4",
                        "entry_id": "96e52e06-381d-3d2d-bbee-33ce13a1ec42",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Hémione (Equus hemionus)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6f33fc24-7bb6-476c-9f84-1f53767e4f20",
                                "sense_id": "d211b040-64ed-3237-bf44-d7648c9fd8f4",
                                "text": "Les Latins, d'après les Grecs, ont appelé l'âne sauvage onager, onagre, qu'il ne faut pas confondre, comme l'ont fait quelques naturalistes et plusieurs voyageurs, avec le zèbre, dont nous donnerons l'histoire à part, parce que le zèbre est un animal d'une espèce différente de celle de l'âne."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eff178c9-4523-4534-b630-5353743b38fd",
                                "sense_id": "d211b040-64ed-3237-bf44-d7648c9fd8f4",
                                "text": "Des troupeaux de chèvres à oreilles tombantes, des moutons à large queue, des ânes qui rappelaient par leur beauté l’onagre des Écritures, sortaient du village au lever de l’aurore."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b25570c5-27f1-4a71-938d-34499d52ecce",
                                "sense_id": "d211b040-64ed-3237-bf44-d7648c9fd8f4",
                                "text": "J’avoue, s’écria l’inconnu, que je ne devine guère le procédé dont on se sera servi pour graver si profondément ces lettres sur la peau d’un onagre."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f7d62997-def7-4b24-a9d0-2d317dc4b8b2",
                                "sense_id": "d211b040-64ed-3237-bf44-d7648c9fd8f4",
                                "text": "« Eh bien, cria le meneur d’ours, direz-vous encore que mon onagre est un âne ? — Non, fit Daniel tout honteux, je vois bien maintenant que c’est un onagre. — À la bonne heure, à la bonne heure. Que d’autres viennent encore combattre cet animal rare, nourri dans les déserts ; qu’ils approchent, l’onagre les attend ! »"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "edeade16-3585-335c-9b12-2e5416bcfd9c",
                        "entry_id": "96e52e06-381d-3d2d-bbee-33ce13a1ec42",
                        "glosses": [
                            "L’onagre de Perse (Equus hemionus onager) est une sous-espèce d’hémione."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "682e2adc-4b39-4c07-85f1-9fc56c08ce57",
                                "sense_id": "edeade16-3585-335c-9b12-2e5416bcfd9c",
                                "text": "Le 18 novembre 1092, Malikshah se trouve au nord de Baghdad, il chasse l’onagre dans une zone boisée et marécageuse. Sur ses douze dernières flèches, une seule a manqué son but, ses compagnons chantent ses louanges, aucun d’eux ne songerait à égaler ses prouesses."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4948a286-c654-3077-a85e-ca5d1a1f3966",
                        "entry_id": "96e52e06-381d-3d2d-bbee-33ce13a1ec42",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Machine de guerre, sorte de baliste, ou de catapulte."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cc668ec5-19a2-4705-b977-744cdf4e23bd",
                        "source_entry_id": "96e52e06-381d-3d2d-bbee-33ce13a1ec42",
                        "source_sense_description": "âne sauvage",
                        "target_lang_word": "Halbesel",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Halbesel",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "79648a01-cc48-3044-a93f-a92ce21698d5",
                                        "entry_id": "b915aea3-8418-3c87-8827-9c7308db2edd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "in Asien heimisches Tier (Unpaarhufer), das mit dem Wildpferd und dem Wildesel verwandt ist und ein braunes oder gelbliches Fell hat sowie einen Quastenschwanz besitzt"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d17023e3-0e16-48c2-80da-5819a213c6b3",
                                                "sense_id": "79648a01-cc48-3044-a93f-a92ce21698d5",
                                                "text": "„Bei den Halbeseln leben Hengste und Stuten in getrennten Rudeln; nur in der Brunftzeit stellen sich die Hengste bei den Stuten ein und fechten untereinander erbitterte Kämpfe aus.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f27ec38f-1ff6-4ea6-8360-fcfa616df87c",
                        "source_entry_id": "96e52e06-381d-3d2d-bbee-33ce13a1ec42",
                        "source_sense_description": "âne sauvage",
                        "target_lang_word": "onager",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "onager",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f9ce8db4-9bc8-3766-9076-1b1cde5b1206",
                                        "entry_id": "390631cd-448d-35a1-99bd-79aa9248639b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The Asiatic wild ass or hemione (Equus hemionus), an animal of the horse family native to Asia; specifically, the Persian onager, Persian wild ass, or Persian zebra (Equus hemionus onager)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d871cfa0-3860-4384-9d36-9418f1e89943",
                                                "sense_id": "f9ce8db4-9bc8-3766-9076-1b1cde5b1206",
                                                "text": "[I]f the czigithai is not the ſame with the zebra, it may be the Aſiatic animal called onager or wild aſs. The onager ſhould not be confounded with the zebra; but I am uncertain whether the ſame remark is applicable to the onager and czigithai; for, from comparing the relations of travellers, it appears, that there are different kinds of wild aſſes, of which the onager is the moſt remarkable. […] The ſwiftneſs of the onager is mentioned by travellers, who remark, that he runs with ſuch rapidity as to eſcape the hunters, though mounted on horſes; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba7feaf9-b45e-4123-a60a-2b1617d6cb51",
                                                "sense_id": "f9ce8db4-9bc8-3766-9076-1b1cde5b1206",
                                                "text": "The onager, or wild aſs, is ſeen in ſtill greater abundance than the wild horſe; and the peculiarities of its kind are more diſtinctly marked than in thoſe of the tame one."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "453beed3-c714-4dff-9f3d-4c9a1ff9897b",
                                                "sense_id": "f9ce8db4-9bc8-3766-9076-1b1cde5b1206",
                                                "text": "One of the onagers, however, having hurt its leg, could not be harnessed at present, and a few days' rest was necessary."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4fec25cf-bb83-3696-b120-75734f99eec3",
                                        "entry_id": "390631cd-448d-35a1-99bd-79aa9248639b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A military engine acting like a sling which threw stones from a bag or wooden bucket powered by the torsion from a bundle of ropes or sinews operated by machinery; a torsion catapult."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5fb26d92-abef-454b-9379-112b2f9ea0de",
                                                "sense_id": "4fec25cf-bb83-3696-b120-75734f99eec3",
                                                "text": "The onager, meaning \"wild ass,\" derived its name from its powerful recoil, or kick, upon discharge; […] In addition, although Josephus described an onager in action hurling a 100-pound stone over 400 yards, most onagri achieved a shorter range than the ballista, thus exposing their crews to enemy archers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "00f6dfdc-df38-420a-a21d-80a2dca24e0c",
                        "source_entry_id": "96e52e06-381d-3d2d-bbee-33ce13a1ec42",
                        "source_sense_description": "âne sauvage",
                        "target_lang_word": "onagro",
